    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0157" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg91"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1831/29: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-29T15:00:00-06:00">September 29, 1934—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>50. Department’s telegram No. 58, September 28, 6 p.m., to Managua.<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d72-f1"/> Minister for Foreign Affairs assures me that legislative
                        <pb facs="0158" n="92" xml:id="pg92"/> approval of proposed trade agreement
                    would be necessary. Congress now meeting in extraordinary session of indefinite
                    duration to which President of Costa Rica could submit agreement by special
                    message. Next regular session convenes May 1st.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sack</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
